From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] client: don't define a "forth" constant

client.fs names the file types of load-state with constants, and the one
for Forth source, "11 constant forth", hides the FORTH vocabulary word
defined in vocabulary.fs. "only forth also definitions" then pushes 0x11
instead of selecting the forth word list. Solaris's kernel debugger
words (data64.fth/kdbg.fth, sent through "interpret") start with that
line and continue with a stray cell on the stack.

Nothing refers to the constant; drop it.
---
 forth/debugging/client.fs | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/forth/debugging/client.fs b/forth/debugging/client.fs
index 5ee6003..c49dd7f 100644
--- a/forth/debugging/client.fs
+++ b/forth/debugging/client.fs
@@ -49,7 +49,8 @@ variable file-size
 4  constant pe
 5  constant aout
 10 constant fcode
-11 constant forth
+\ 11 is a Forth source file: no constant for it, the name would hide
+\ the FORTH vocabulary word ("only forth also definitions")
 12 constant bootcode
 13 constant prep
 
